  "releaseNotes": "**feat(jsonpath): add optional unquote support for string values**\n\n      * Added optional `unquote` parameter to `JsonPath.Find()`.\n      * Preserves backward compatibility by returning the original JSON value by default.\n      * When `unquote` is `true`, string values are returned without the surrounding double quotes.\n      * Simplifies direct string comparisons without requiring additional slicing by the caller.\n\n      Example:\n\n      ```csharp\n      JsonPath.Find(json, \"username\"u8);        // => \"\\\"admin\\\"\"\n      JsonPath.Find(json, \"username\"u8, true);  // => \"admin\"\n      ```",
